# Nimpass root ignore rules.
#
# The repository is public (docs/09-SECURITY.md §28), so anything committed
# here must be assumed readable by an attacker. These rules implement §29
# (secrets never committed) and §30 (the .env rule) repository-wide; the
# backend/ and frontend/web/ ignore files only cover their own subtrees and
# their /.env anchors do not reach nested directories.

# --- Secrets: environment files, at any depth -------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example
!*.env.example
!.env.sample

# --- Secrets: key and certificate material ----------------------------------
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.cer
*.der
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
*.asc
*.gpg
*.kdbx
id_rsa
id_rsa.*
id_ed25519
id_ed25519.*
*.ppk
secrets/
.secrets/
*.secrets.json
service-account*.json
gha-creds-*.json

# --- Wallet material: must never exist in this repo at all ------------------
# Nimpass never receives or stores private wallet keys (docs/09-SECURITY.md
# §205). These patterns are a backstop against an accidental local file, not
# a licence to keep one.
*.seed
*.mnemonic
wallet.json
keystore/
*.nimiq-key

# --- Database dumps and local data ------------------------------------------
# Migrations under backend/migrations/*.sql stay tracked; only dumps/backups
# are ignored, so *.sql is deliberately NOT listed here.
*.dump
*.sql.gz
*.sql.bz2
*.sql.zst
dump.sql
*-dump.sql
*_dump.sql
*.bak
*.backup
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
/dumps/
/backups/

# --- Dependencies and build output ------------------------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
dist-ssr/
build/
.vite/
.turbo/
*.local

# --- Go build and test artifacts --------------------------------------------
/bin/
*.test
*.out
coverage/
coverage.*
!coverage.config.*

# --- Logs --------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# --- OS and editor noise -----------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*.sw?
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json

# --- AI agent tooling (local developer setup, not part of the deliverable) --
# Kept out of the public competition repository by choice. Using AI tools is
# explicitly allowed with no disclosure requirement (docs/06-COMPETITION.md
# §24), so nothing here is required for submission. docs/ remains the
# implementation contract and stays tracked.
.agents/
.claude/
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
skills-lock.json
